# Extended runtime contract

Read this only when the injected leaf adapter identifies a transition,
implementation/review orchestration, consumed handoff, or host-specific
prerequisite. Ordinary single-skill work already has the core contract
inline.

The bundled upstream module supplies the method, not authority to override the
user, higher-priority instructions, or the current project's rules. Do not
force a whole flow when one phase solves the request.

When a module names another `/skill`, resolve it by reading the sibling
`../<skill>/SKILL.md` from the bundle only when that sibling exists.
Otherwise treat the name as a host built-in (for example `/compact`) or prose,
not a broken skill transition. Load a sibling only when the transition is
reached. A wrapper that merely delegates does not create a second completion
claim.

Before acting:

- Determine a concrete, checkable completion criterion from the module's
  promised result. If none is explicit, state the smallest faithful criterion.
- For `specialty`, `environment-bound`, `experimental`, `legacy`, or
  host-specific modules, read [host adapters](host-adapters.md) and verify the
  prerequisite first.
- Do not force `setup-matt-pocock-skills` merely because optional project
  configuration is absent. Use current repo evidence and the donor's local
  defaults when they preserve the request; load setup only when configuration
  is itself requested or a required branch cannot be chosen safely.
- Treat external messages or tracker writes, dependency installation, commits,
  pushes, branch operations, destructive actions, and edits outside the user's
  scope as side effects. Perform them only when the request authorizes or
  clearly entails them; otherwise stop at the boundary with the useful local
  result intact. Preserve unrelated work.
- If a module will edit the repo and later transition to `code-review`, capture
  the pre-change `HEAD` before the first edit. The review must include the full
  WIP described in `host-adapters.md`, even when no commit is authorized.

Verify the completion criterion before claiming success. Missing tools,
references, permissions, or required artifacts are `blocked`, not simulated
success.

A pure delegating wrapper does not create a second completion claim.

For `handoff` or `claude-handoff`, also read and satisfy the
[handoff contract](handoff-contract.md) before claiming completion.
When consuming an existing handoff, validate it before loading any suggested
skill. Keep its `Handoff-ID`; missing or invalid input is
`blocked/handoff_invalid`, not a request to create a replacement handoff.

